Pass $event as context to hook_recurring_events_event_instance_alter(), and drop
moderation_state before adding a translation.

1. EventCreationService::createEventInstance() invokes the alter with only the
   $data array, so an implementation cannot tell which series an instance is
   being created for. access_events needs that context to decide the birth state
   of the instance (a published parent yields a published instance).

2. When translating a series, $data still carries the moderation_state computed
   for the default-language instance. Passing it into addTranslation() re-runs
   the content_moderation transition against the translation and can reset the
   instance state. Unset it so the translation inherits the default revision's
   state instead.

Still required as of 3.0.0.

--- a/src/EventCreationService.php
+++ b/src/EventCreationService.php
@@ -496,7 +496,7 @@
       'uid' => $event->getOwnerId(),
     ];
 
-    $this->moduleHandler->alter('recurring_events_event_instance', $data);
+    $this->moduleHandler->alter('recurring_events_event_instance', $data, $event);
 
     $storage = $this->entityTypeManager->getStorage('eventinstance');
     $entity = NULL;
@@ -524,6 +524,10 @@
         $entity = $storage->load(reset($entity_ids));
         // Only add a translation if we do not already have one.
         if (!$entity->hasTranslation($event->language()->getId())) {
+          // The moderation state of the default-language instance governs the
+          // whole entity; passing it into addTranslation() re-runs the
+          // content_moderation state transition and can reset the instance.
+          unset($data['moderation_state']);
           $entity->addTranslation($event->language()->getId(), $data);
         }
       }
